      "citation_relevance": 1.0,
      "answer_text": "When the max-age directive appears in a request, it indicates that the client prefers a response whose age is less than or equal to the specified number of seconds, and unless the max-stale request directive is also present, the client does not wish to receive a stale response (RFC 9111 \u00a75.2.1.1).\n\nWhen the max-age directive appears in a response, it indicates that the response is to be considered stale after its age is greater than the specified number of seconds (RFC 9111 \u00a75.2.2.1)."
