      "citation_relevance": 0.0,
      "answer_text": "An HTTP/3 connection can end in two distinct ways: \n\n1. Abrupt closure initiated by the transport, as described in RFC 9114 \u00a75 Connection Closure. \n2. Graceful closure initiated by the application, also described in RFC 9114 \u00a75 Connection Closure.\n\nThe abrupt closure initiated by the transport does not allow the application to complete any remaining tasks, whereas the graceful closure initiated by the application allows the application to complete any necessary remaining tasks. \n\nRFC 9114 \u00a75 Connection Closure."
    },
