      "answer_text": "The chunked transfer coding structures the body of a message as a series of chunks, each with its own size indicator, followed by an OPTIONAL trailer section containing trailer fields. The structure is as follows:\n\nchunked-body = *chunk last-chunk trailer-section CRLF\n\nchunk = chunk-size [ chunk-ext ] CRLF chunk-data CRLF\nchunk-size = 1*HEXDIG\nlast-chunk = 1*(\"0\") [ chunk-ext ] CRLF\nchunk-data = 1*OCTET; a sequence of chunk-size octets\n\nRFC 9112 \u00a77.1"
